      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-372",
      "replacement_bytes": 328,
      "replacement_sha256": "E39AD90A68D6FD180FA797828116A18E07A1B86BE3B43019B0E9634C24323B9A",
      "replacement_text": "$\\mathfrak p \\subset R$ is a prime, then for every $i$ such that\n$f_i \\not \\in \\mathfrak p$ we see\n$R_{f_i}/\\mathfrak pR_{f_i} = (R/\\mathfrak p)_{f_i}$ is N-2.\nThe images of these $f_i$ in $R/\\mathfrak p$ generate the unit ideal, and\nhence we conclude $R/\\mathfrak p$ is N-2 by\nLemma \\ref{lemma-Japanese-local}. This proves (2).",
      "source_end_line": 45751,
      "source_start_line": 45748,
      "stable_id": "MC-STK-ERR-0715",
      "start_byte": 1689598
    },
    {
