      "old_sha256": "9D55E4180F915BC2BB226566F18E8405CA8F777E5CEF2ED9D2B3239277381754",
      "old_text": "$B = A[x]/(x^p - a)$ is a domain because $K[x]/(x^p - a)$ is a field.",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-381",
      "replacement_bytes": 282,
      "replacement_sha256": "CD44B00C7DAEC537B3199413F8EE4EA620A469FF11DD8648280E5659AB0952EA",
      "replacement_text": "$B = A[x]/(x^p - a)$ is a domain because $K[x]/(x^p - a)$ is a field.\nThe ring $B$ is local because its special fibre\n$B/\\mathfrak mB = \\kappa(\\mathfrak m)[x]/(x^p - \\overline{a})$ has a unique\nprime ideal. Moreover, the maximal-adic and $\\mathfrak mB$-adic topologies\non $B$ agree.",
